A||||7||Standard||Fiero Sightings and some racing||||6||
Z||000000||Standard||09-18-2000||02:56 PM||||Friday was a pretty good day, left to go to my g/f's house and saw a perfect gold GT fastback at the stoplight on duluth street, about 3 blocks from my house.  He waved and I gave him a thumbs up.  Good start for the day  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif">  Then close to my g/f's I saw a shiny red GT fastback.. make's me a little embarassed about havin' a dirty GT  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/redface.gif"><P>Later on that night, I got to race a newer Dodge Neon "sport", at least that's what I think it was.  All I could tell is that it was a 99 or '00 dodge and had a sport badge on the front quarter.  He was next to me at a left turn light, but I wasn't sure if he was gonna race or not.  I took off anyways but he didn't quite follow my lead.  The next light was red, he was in the far right lane, and I was in the middle lane.  I had to get in his lane to take an exit, and I'm sure he didn't want to let me.  Light turns green and I bring it up to 3k and got the jump on him.  I hear his tires start squalling about when the nose of his car was at my passenger side door.  I still beat him by about a carlength up to 50  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif">  Got on the exit and I was hoping for him to follow me onto the highway but no go.<P>While I'm motoring down the highway at about 70 (speed limit 65) I come across a late 70's camaro/firebird. I can never tell the difference..  But he had some meaty tires on the back and traction bars, and I could hear a nice rumble when I passed him.  I get a little ahead of him, and all of the sudden he comes roaring by, and slows down again a little ahead of me.  It's on  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/wink.gif">  <BR>I was sure that I didn't stand much of a chance against him, but I wanted some excitment.  We both slow down to about 55 and I'm ready to drop it in 3rd.  I'm not sure who got the jump, but we took it up to 80-85 and although he was pulling away, he was doing it pretty slowly.  The nose of my car was about at his rear bumper.  A lot better than I thought I would do so I was plenty happy.  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif">  There was some traffic up ahead so we got through that and I tried to line up again, but as soon as I got next to him he punched it.. I wasn't ready so I let him go.  My exit was coming up pretty soon but I figured I'd try one last time, so I got beside him and threw it in 3rd at about 65 to see if he would bite, but no go.  Either his car wasn't as fast as it sounded, or he wasn't trying too hard.  Still got the adrenalin going  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"><P>------------------<BR>Mike -<BR>Black 86.5 GT 5 Spd, 150,000 miles and counting!       <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/BURNOUT.gif">    <BR>Red 84 Sport Coupe - winter donut maker||||reg||6
Z||000001||ThatRickGuy||09-18-2000||07:07 PM||||don't go blaspheming old pontiacs. if it was a slowmaro, I don't mind. But the old Pontiacs are some great cars, altho, out on the highway, already cruising at 70 isn't really great terrain for them. Pontiac made some wickedly torqued engines, so sure, you can olny spin a 450 to 5500 rpms, but you're putting out a butt load of torque. So, you could only top out a bit over a hundred, but you can hit the 60' mark in 2 seconds or less.  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"> ||||reg||1
Z||000002||DjKid||09-18-2000||09:04 PM||||Ya know man, Standard, I got one thing to tell ya.. STOMP THE SORRY NEONS!!!! I feel like  a big ole monkey been lifted off my back. I hate neons and feel bad whenever I see one  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/frown.gif">||||reg||1
Z||000003||Standard||09-19-2000||07:01 PM||||Wow Dj, what do you have against Neon's?<P>------------------<BR>Mike -<BR>Black 86.5 GT 5 Spd, 150,000 miles and counting!       <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/BURNOUT.gif">    <BR>Red 84 Sport Coupe - winter donut maker||||reg||1
